  "annotations_dropped": [
    {
      "annotation_id": "a8df6486dda0474896eda2b281f48fea_13",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "5. Having considered the submissions advanced on behalf of the parties, a perusal of the record reflects that vide impugned order an application filed under Section 5 of the Limitation Act along with the Memorandum of Appeal before the Food"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7d67889870914f30830b3cf527460658_14",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Perusal of the order passed by the Tribunal reflects that the appeal was required to be filed as per Article 116 of Schedule I of Limitation Act,\n1963 within a period of 30 days from the date of the order passed by the Adjudicating Authorit"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e6f7d4fe2d45417081a1bb2a78345dd0_15",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The Adjudicating Authority passed the order on 17.4.2023 and the appeal was preferred on 8.6.2023."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b6fce2dbf6ff46859315687516ddc4cc_16",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nTherefore, the record reflects that there was delay of approximately one month and few days in filing the appeal."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9d74461458274673bac48944749c81f4_17",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is also evident from perusal of Section 71 (6) of the Act of 2006 that the provisions of Limitation Act are applicable to an appeal which is preferred to a Tribunal in terms of the provisions of Act of 2006."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f003a14314544f38ad4b0857c640b287_18",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Therefore, the application under Section 5 of Limitation Act was required to be dealt with by the Tribunal in its right perspective."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d955fd56509642728e739d69e428aaf4_19",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is settled proposition of law that the Rules of Limitations are not meant to destroy the substantive rights of the parties unless parties take recourse to dilatory tactics."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e47c78bed389437da922414de0502832_20",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In the present case, it was specifically stated in the NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2024:MPHC-JBP:47166 3 CRR-1812-2024 application for condonation of delay that the petitioner came to know about passing of the order of Adjudicating Authority dated"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "345162487ccb46f789ca272f40f5ef93_21",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "6. The Apex Court in the case of N. Balakrishnan vs. M. Krishnamurthy (1998) 7 SCC 123 in para 10 and 11 has held as under :\n\"10."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f996fbcef8a9421fb35b15634926ca9f_22",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The reason for such a different stance is thus:\nThe primary function of a court is to adjudicate the dispute between the parties and to advance substantial justice."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "cfaa73e22dbc4289a977276d7a30dd50_23",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The time-limit fixed for approaching the court in different situations is not because on the expiry of such time a bad cause would transform into a good cause."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d654ee0bff544c8e86942390270febfc_24",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n11. Rules of limitation are not meant to destroy the rights of parties."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "51da0149336d4ec192d3516b466a50ff_25",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "They are meant to see that parties do not resort to dilatory tactics, but seek their remedy promptly."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c8265b20da404e98bb47bba48265b6a3_26",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nThe object of providing a legal remedy is to repair the damage caused by reason of legal injury."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b7150b2a72754221907c6eb3830b114a_27",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The law of limitation fixes a lifespan for such legal remedy for the redress of the legal injury so suffered."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "02af431036504309b9d6d03c6ad4f1ad_28",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Time is precious and wasted time would never revisit."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1ba4948f16554a1d820972879c61deea_29",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nDuring the efflux of time, newer causes would sprout up necessitating newer persons to seek legal remedy by approaching the courts."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ce61672eb2ac480191fc0acec852b79e_30",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "So a lifespan must be fixed for each remedy."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "09500b112e9644619e5ec9b7047cbf3a_31",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Unending period for launching the remedy may lead to unending uncertainty and consequential anarchy."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "2a486f86f09445efb769eb37aa87e43e_32",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The law of limitation is thus founded on public policy."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6013d658e23a49abbbfed744380bc64c_33",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It is enshrined in the maxim interest reipublicae up sit finis litium (it is for the general welfare that a period be put to litigation)."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5dd4ce9a4bfc40e1a04b2a74385ceac0_34",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nRules of limitation are not meant to destroy the rights of the parties."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3ec8c39c5478487ea12ccfa45371b726_35",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "They are meant to see that parties do not resort to dilatory tactics but seek their remedy promptly."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "01a9c3d425a54b39889cf5199021d086_36",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The idea is that every legal remedy must be kept alive for a legislatively fixed period of time.\"\nRaman Yadav vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 17 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/163958559/\n2 7."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6c2edf4cfb9f46aa8b5bdcc75acb42a4_37",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In view of the aforesaid law laid down by the Apex Court, it is apparent NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2024:MPHC-JBP:47166 4 CRR-1812-2024 that the Rules of Limitations are not meant to destroy the substantive right of the parties."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c6040c16b07c472e901c31fbc750c128_38",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The right of filing an appeal in terms of provisions of Act of 2006 is statutory right of the present petitioner."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "90f9c0c03ab440a8b87f854f39f69ef5_39",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Even otherwise the delay was also not inordinate."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4ee5f096088e40edbe1d5a15162f52c1_40",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nTherefore, the Tribunal ought to have resorted to a lenient approach in the present case and ought to have allowed the application for condonation of delay."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b5fa655e133f429292adf85014a47d74_41",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "8. Thus, this Court is of the considered view that upon condonation of delay, the appeal is required to be heard on merit."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "15ff6abbe8fb418d8a2c4d9538e05c82_42",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "9. Resultantly, the present Revision stands allowed."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "01c03bb5469049be80aed1e3ea6d6f5a_43",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
